{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A retry loop with no visible running cost doesn't fail loud — it quietly compounds until the invoice shows up.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Track cost per session live, surface it in the UI, and set a hard cap that degrades gracefully — cheaper model at a warning threshold, blocked calls at the limit.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Scope the cap to the session, check it between individual tool calls rather than full turns, and enforce it server-side — a UI meter alone is visibility, not a spend control.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
